course: dictionary
lesson: 4925
title: Impairment and respectful words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An impairment is a problem with part of the body or mind that makes it work less well. «Hearing impairment» means a problem with hearing, and «visual impairment» means a problem with seeing.
explain: Use the context to check. «Goalball is played 3 against 3 by athletes with visual impairments; everyone wears eyeshades so it is fair.» The eyeshades are a clue: the game is set up for players who cannot see well. Ask yourself what word would fit, then put your meaning into the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
explain: Talk about people with care and respect. Name the kind of impairment in plain words, like «visual impairment», and focus on what helps someone take part, not on the person as a problem.
fact: An impairment is a problem with part of the body or mind that makes it work less well.
fact: «Hearing impairment» means a problem with hearing.
fact: «Visual impairment» means a problem with seeing.
fact: Impairment can also mean the state of being damaged or weakened.
fact: Paralympians are grouped into classes by their kind of impairment so that races are fair.
exercise: «Goalball is played by athletes with visual impairments.» What kind of impairment is this? | A problem with speaking | *A problem with seeing | A problem with sleeping | A problem with hearing
exercise: «Paralympians are grouped into classes by their kind of impairment so races are fair.» Why are they grouped this way? | So that they can sleep longer | *So that races are fair | So that the ball has bells inside | So that the races are shorter
exercise: Which phrase names a problem with hearing? | eyeshades | bells inside the ball | goalball | *hearing impairment
test:
Ella says impairment means a fun game with a ball. What does impairment really mean? | *A problem that makes part of the body or mind work less well | A game played with a ball | A kind of bell | A type of race
What does «sight impairment» tell you? | *A problem with eyesight | A problem with teeth | A problem with feet | A problem with a bicycle
exam:
Which word fits the gap in «Goalball players wear eyeshades because of their visual ____»? | *impairments | finals | bells | distances
